# Cursor AI Rules for ADML

## Project Context
ADML is the AI-Generated Dynamical Model Library - a collection of FMI 3.0 compliant dynamical models implemented entirely by AI agents.

## Key Files
- `AGENTS.md` - Quick reference for AI agents
- `docs/AI_QUICK_START.md` - Step-by-step guide
- `docs/AI_AGENTS.md` - Comprehensive implementation guide
- `docs/AI_SCAFFOLDING.md` - Copy-paste templates
- `docs/ERROR_CATALOG.md` - Error solutions

## Critical Conventions

### Naming
- Struct name: CamelCase from directory (my-model → MyModel)
- Package name: adml-{model-name} (lowercase with hyphens)

### FMI Variables
- `#[fmu_from_struct(parameter)]` - Can be set before simulation
- `#[fmu_from_struct(output)]` - Appears in simulation results

### Integration
- Use Euler with step_size ≤ 0.01
- Tolerance 5% for short simulations, 10-25% for long

## Required Imports
```rust
#![allow(clippy::not_unsafe_ptr_arg_deref)]
#![allow(clippy::ptr_offset_with_cast)]
pub use fmu_from_struct::prelude::*;
```

## Commands
- `cargo test -p adml-{model}` - Test single model
- `./scripts/build-fmu.sh models/{category}/{model}` - Build FMU
- `cargo fmt && cargo clippy` - Format and lint

## Don't Forget
1. Add model to workspace in root Cargo.toml
2. Struct name must match directory pattern exactly
3. Only outputs appear in simulation results
4. Use small step sizes for Euler accuracy
